# Nabad Vibe — hidden in code, one command to test

Vibe **lives on `staging` and `main`** (UI + API) but is **invisible** until launched.

## Hidden by default (safe for TestFlight / main)

| Gate | Default |
|---|---|
| `NABAD_VIBE_PUBLIC_SHIPPED` in `src/feature-flags.js` | **`false`** — must stay false until explicit launch |
| Phone/simulator bake | `nabadVibeUi: false` unless `NABAD_VIBE_UI=1` |
| Who sees UI when hidden | **Admin only**, and only with UI bake flag |
| Production API | `NABAD_VIBE_ENABLED` **off** on nabadai.com |
| Staging API | `NABAD_VIBE_ENABLED=1` on Vercel Preview |

Before **every push to `main`**: `npm run verify:no-producer-ship` (checks Producer + Vibe flags).

## Daily workflow

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Normal fixes (simulator) | `git checkout staging` → `npm run sim` |
| Sami's phone — Vibe testing | `npm run run:ios:vibe` |
| Ship fixes to production | staging → main (verify flags still false) |

**One command for Vibe on phone:** `npm run run:ios:vibe`
(staging API + admin account + Vibe UI flag baked in)

## When Sami is ready to launch Vibe publicly

1. Set `NABAD_VIBE_PUBLIC_SHIPPED = true` in `src/feature-flags.js`
2. Enable `NABAD_VIBE_ENABLED=1` on **production** Vercel
3. Ship to main + TestFlight with explicit approval (user must say by name: ship feature Vibe)

## Agent rules

- **Do not** remove Vibe code from staging/main to "hide" it — use the flag.
- **Do not** set `NABAD_VIBE_PUBLIC_SHIPPED = true` without explicit user approval.
- Vibe is **inspiration only** — never copy lyrics/melody from uploads (prompt + UI disclaimers).
